WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.740
Security is the common criterion included in every SOC 2 engagement.

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:12.760
It focuses on protecting systems against unauthorized access, misuse, disruption, modification, and disclosure.

3
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:23.040
Security controls may include access management, monitoring, vulnerability management, incident response, change control, and risk management practices.

4
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.880
Security is foundational because many other trust objectives depend on it.

5
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:35.260
Confidential information cannot be protected without security controls, and availability can suffer when systems are not monitored or maintained.

6
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:47.860
For engineering teams, security often appears in daily work through identity management, secure configuration, patching, review processes, logging, alerting, and disciplined change management.
